{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "11edcc18-2d7d-4953-b232-709864d3812e",
    "name": "Umbrella DCP Data Transfer - Per-Participant IdentityHub",
    "description": "End-to-end Decentralized Claims Protocol (DCP) data-transfer demonstration for the Tractus-X umbrella IdentityHub PER-PARTICIPANT profile (charts/values-test-data-exchange-identity-hub-per-participant.yaml): provider and consumer1 each on their own IdentityHub.\\n\\nSINGLE FILE - all variables live in this collection (Variables tab); there is NO separate environment to import. Run the folders in order (or use the Collection Runner with a ~2000ms delay). The provider provisions data/asset/policies/contract; the consumer runs catalog -> negotiation -> transfer -> fetch. Test scripts thread the variables automatically (offer_id -> negotiation_id -> transfer_process_id -> edr_endpoint + edr_token). Steps 8/9/10 self-poll via pm.execution.setNextRequest; step 9 re-negotiates once on the cold-BDRS-cache race (matches hack/dcp-data-transfer-smoke.sh). A green run ends with the fetched payload containing data_marker.\\n\\nBy default `ingress_ip`=127.0.0.1 routes via the kind ingress with a Host header (no /etc/hosts needed); clear it to use real DNS. For the SHARED or POSTGRES profile, change only provider_did to did:web:identity-hub.tx.test:BPNL00000003AYRE. SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Optional: when `ingress_ip` is set, connect to that IP and carry the real",
          "// vhost as a Host header (ingress-nginx routes by Host). Lets the collection",
          "// run without /etc/hosts entries, mirroring the smoke test's INGRESS_IP.",
          "const ip = pm.variables.get('ingress_ip');",
          "if (ip) {",
          "  const resolved = pm.variables.replaceIn(pm.request.url.toString());",
          "  const m = resolved.match(/^(https?):\\/\\/([^\\/:]+)(?::(\\d+))?([\\s\\S]*)$/);",
          "  if (m && m[2] !== ip) {",
          "    pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Host', value: m[2] });",
          "    pm.request.url = m[1] + '://' + ip + (m[3] ? ':' + m[3] : '') + (m[4] || '');",
          "  }",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
